Nov 2025

This file summarizes various bugs and workarounds

1: As detailed in TLDR.md, Chrome and Firefox do not work
(sometimes) when libtrash is preloaded. These browsers
should be loaded with the command: LD_PRELOAD= browser_command.
Nearly 20 years of review cannot fix this.

2: As outlined in Issue #7, programs that operate recursively
may fail when libtrash is preloaded. The program lua fails in
certain circumstances. A thorough review by the maintainer
verified the issue but has no fix in the pipeline. Again,
LD_PRELOAD= lua_command should be used.

3: As outlined in Issue #8, It appears the PROTECT_TRASH
variable cannot be unset. The maintainer has verified this
but it remains unclear what the original developer intended.
I believe that if libtrash is activated, the TRASH folder
should be protected. See libtrash.conf.5 manpage for more
info. This could be an omission or a bug or a documentation
error. Best practice is to use TRASH_OFF=YES rm TRASH/file.

Peter Hyman
